# Motoko Backend Engineering Standards

## Skills in this set

| Skill | Load when |
|---|---|
| `writing-motoko` | Writing or reviewing any `.mo` file |
| `testing-motok` | Writing or running tests, verifying upgrade persistence |
| `cycles-and-cost` | Optimizing, choosing query vs update, sizing runway |
| `ledger-integration` | Code that holds or moves ICP |
| `internet-identity-auth` | Login, delegations, session restore |
| `migrating-motoko` | Inline migration, no `--enhanced-migration` |
| `migrating-motoko-enhanced` | `migrations/` directory projects |
| `deploy-guide/` | Building, deploying, upgrading (read `README.md` first) |
| `build-and-test`, `bump-*` | Only inside the dfinity/motoko compiler repo |

## Objective
Build production-grade ICP canisters with clean architecture, strong separation of concerns, deterministic behavior, scalability, maintainability, and security.

## Core Principles
- Prefer simplicity over cleverness.
- Prefer readability over brevity.
- Prefer explicit behavior over hidden behavior.
- Prefer composition over duplication.
- Every file must have a single responsibility.
- Every module must have a clear owner.
- Business logic must never leak into controllers.
- Stable memory access must be isolated.
- Public APIs must remain backward compatible.

## Architecture Rules
### Layer Order
Controllers -> Services -> Repositories -> Storage

Allowed: Controller -> Service, Service -> Repository, Repository -> Storage
Forbidden: Controller -> Storage, Controller -> Repository, Storage -> Controller, Storage -> Service, Repository -> Controller

## Folder Ownership
### api/  : Request handling, response mapping, route exposure. No business/validation/storage logic.
### services/ : Business rules, workflow orchestration, domain logic. No stable memory access, no HTTP concerns.
### repositories/ : Data access abstraction, CRUD. No business rules.
### storage/ : Stable memory, persistence, serialization. No business decisions.
### models/ : Domain entities.
### dto/ : API contracts, request/response models.
### validators/ : Input validation, business validation.
### utils/ : Pure helper functions.

## Naming Standards
- Files: PascalCase (RoundService.mo)
- Variables: camelCase (currentRound)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (MIN_ENTRY_ICP)
- Functions: camelCase verbs (createRound, joinRound, drawWinners)

## Error Handling
Never trap for expected errors. Use Result types: #ok(...) / #err("message")

## Security Rules
Never trust frontend data. Always verify: caller identity, transfer amount, round state, duplicate participation, prize eligibility.
All winner selection must use ICP randomness: raw_rand(). Never time/local/seeded/deterministic.

## API Versioning
Always expose APIs under version folders: api/v1/. Never break existing API contracts.

## Testing Rules
Every service must have tests. Required: happy path, invalid input, duplicate entry, closed round, winner draw, prize payout, upgrade persistence.

## Upgrade Safety
All critical state must survive upgrades: rounds, entries, winners, treasury, statistics. State loss = critical failure.

## Golden Rule
Write code that a new engineer can understand in under five minutes without explanation.
